   "definition_quote": "the environment decides $T$ reward functions $f_1, \\ldots, f_T: \\Pi \\to [0,1]$ unknown to the learner. Then, in each round $t = 1, \\ldots, T$, the learner chooses a policy $\\pi_t\\in\\Pi$ and receives a noisy reward $R_t \\in [0,1]$ whose mean is $f_t(\\pi_t)$. The dynamic regret of the learner is defined as $\\Regret = \\sum_{t=1}^T \\left(f^\\star_t - R_t\\right)$"
  },
